viz: vector index chart — removes the last bitmap and the last flicker source

Follow-up to v0.10.28. Two composer charts still flickered on hover;
neither for the reason it looked like.

## The histogram flickered because of its neighbour

It is built from plain divs and touches no bitmap. Two separate causes,
neither in its own drawing:

1. The index chart beside it was the last RenderImage in the console.
   GPUI re-renders the whole view on any cx.notify(), so hovering a
   histogram *bar* re-rasterised the *index chart*, leaking a sprite
   atlas tile per mouse-move. The histogram looked like it flickered;
   its neighbour was doing it.

2. Both charts had a readout above them that grew on hover — one line to
   six for the histogram, one to four for the index chart — inside a
   flex column. Hovering pushed the chart down, out from under the
   cursor, clearing the hover, shrinking the readout, moving the chart
   back up. A self-sustaining layout oscillation, visually identical to
   flicker and independent of the atlas leak.

Both readouts are now a fixed two lines at fixed height.

## The index chart wasn't drawing what it claimed

It plotted three "series", but the base rate and crowd price were copied
unchanged into every version row — two constants given the same visual
weight as the one line that varied. That is why it did not read like the
trajectory chart: it was not drawing the same kind of thing.

Now the crowd is a real series, sampled from recorded price history at
each version's timestamp; the base rate is drawn as the level it is; the
model–crowd gap is shaded; revisions that moved the number carry a delta
badge; and hover is continuous rather than N invisible per-version
columns.

events::sample_within returns None outside the recorded span rather than
clamping — a version saved before polling began shows "crowd —", not
today's price wearing last week's date.

## No bitmaps remain

charts.rs deleted. plotters, plotters-bitmap, ab_glyph,
ab_glyph_rasterizer, owned_ttf_parser and image dropped from the
console's dependency tree. With no RenderImage left in the application
this class of flicker is not fixed so much as structurally unavailable.

131 lib tests, up from 118 — including the version-pixel round trip,
snap-to-nearest-version, and the refusal to extrapolate crowd prices.

See docs/fermi/VISUALIZATION_ARCHITECTURE.md.
